      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Altogether 32 patients were investigated by catheterization of the left ventricular cavity with volume loading of 76% solution of verographin++ administered at 0.65 ml per kg body mass. beta-blockade with preliminary i.v. administration of 5 mg obsidan or 10 mg cordanum was shown to improve myocardial diastolic function as a result of improved myocardial distensibility in CHD patients."},
